From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:31:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipip: drop the CAP_NET_ADMIN check misplaced into
 ipip_newlink()

The base carries upstream commit 8211a2632466 ("net: ipip: require
CAP_NET_ADMIN in the device netns for changelink") twice. Ubuntu commit
3302cb2aedce applies it to ipip_changelink() as upstream does, while
2a76937e1cd9 from the 43.43i1 security sweep left its hunk where the
context matched in this tree, in ipip_newlink().

In ipip_newlink() the tunnel is not set up yet and t->net is NULL, so
creating any ipip device dereferences a NULL pointer with RTNL held,
which hangs all networking of the host. Root in an unprivileged
container can trigger this too, as the ipip module gets loaded on
demand.

Drop the misplaced copy, the check in ipip_changelink() stays.

Link: https://bugzilla.proxmox.com/show_bug.cgi?id=8264
Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
---
 net/ipv4/ipip.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/ipv4/ipip.c b/net/ipv4/ipip.c
index 7529d51e4b31b70c52375b76019021807d64bf9e..06274ec811c3d579db0baa698d88389338bd425e 100644
--- a/net/ipv4/ipip.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/ipip.c
@@ -714,9 +714,6 @@ static int ipip_newlink(struct net_device *dev,
 	__u32 fwmark = 0;
 	int err;
 
-	if (!rtnl_dev_link_net_capable(dev, t->net))
-		return -EPERM;
-
 	if (ip_tunnel_netlink_encap_parms(data, &ipencap)) {
 		err = ip_tunnel_encap_setup(t, &ipencap);
 
